From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:33:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: VM, retirement, TVB and submission updates
 (2026-10-03)

- rust/drm: GEM import arguments for shmem objects; G16 imports DMA-BUFs
- VM: vmalloc-backed mapping list; binds replace overlapping ranges; unmap
  reserves at most one split record and skips holes
- queue storage recycling after firmware context destruction
- retirement: one scan retires every finished flight; notification-wait
  timeout polls retirement so the watchdog runs
- cached support page with an uncached per-lease render shared state;
  compute timestamp pointers in uncached memory
- TVB: lease all 80 scene records in order; growth factor 3
- render: bank tag for 128-byte samples at every sample count
- submission as macOS: shared notifier per lane, no per-Work profiling
  stamps, notifier flush flag 0 (currently behind module parameters)
- hang dumps; firmware fault/timeout events fail the device; re-kick removed
- experiment module parameters (micro_layout, work_layout, region_c_layout,
  perf_base, render_barrier, dependency_kind, tvb_growth) and fw_trace bits
  16-128, to be dropped or decided in the reorganization

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RvQieG9SGoR3ZeSdSguHnB
(cherry picked from commit 7d4448f681720d97d9b46c239bd55d138f850f79; G16 driver files only: rust/kernel/drm changes ported separately in this branch)
